Kf7 32. Bc3 Qxe4 { Black won very easily. } ) 
10. Qxg7+ Kxg7 11. Bd4+ Kf8 12. Ba1 { And we reach an interesting endgame where White’s pieces are more or less tied down, but it is hard to break through the defence. An attempt to win could be: } e6 { Opening lines. } 13. Kg1 ( { But not } 32. dxe6 $2 fxe6 33. Bxe6 Re8 34. Bc4 { due to } d5 $1 { -+ and the back rank is defenceless after } 35. Bxd5 ( 35. exd5 $2 Re1 ) 
