 { Asymmetric Transformation Once the knight on d5 is captured, White can also recapture exd5 to obtain a very different kind of position, which we call the asymmetric transformation of the Maroczy. Unlike the symmetric transformation, the recapture exd5 is much more tactical and double-edged. White typically attempts a mating attack while Black will gain counterplay on the queenside. Black has a backward pawn on e7 which could become a target for White's rooks. However, Black can often neutralize this pressure by simply placing his dark-squared bishop on f6. White's plans 1. Create a kingside attack with the break f2-f4-f5 . 2. Pressure the e7-pawn by doubling rooks on the e-file. This is only likely to work if Black cannot place a bishop on f6. Black's plans 1. Attack White's c4-d5 chain with the break ...b7-b5xc4. 2. Open the a-file with ...a7-a5-a4xb3. If White responds to ...a5-a4 with b3-b4, then the c4-d5 chain becomes weaker, and the break ...b7-b5 could be stronger. 3. Simplify the position to minimize White's attacking chances. White's kingside attack is very effective if Black cannot create the appropriate distraction with queenside play. For this reason, it is a must for Black to have at least one queenside break at hand. In contrast, if Black realizes he will not be able to find a queenside break, then he should probably avoid this structure altogether, or find a way to swap queens before an attack develops. If Black desires to press for a win, the best approach is to combine Plans 1-3 (or 2-3), when trading queens is most important. Once Black has played ...b7-b5xc4, and White recaptures b3xc4, then the c4-pawn becomes a serious longterm target. This weakness is often more serious than Black's e7-pawn which is easily defended by a bishop on f6 or a king on f8. The next example will show us the power of White's kingside attack once Black has missed the opportunity to achieve a queenside break. Then, we will see a short fragment to illustrate the ease of Black's play in an endgame, once the c4-pawn has been weakened. }  
 *

